NNAAMMEE
       pickup - Postfix local mail pickup

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppiicckkuupp [generic Postfix daemon options]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ppiicckkuupp(8)  daemon  waits  for hints that new mail has been dropped
       into the mmaaiillddrroopp directory, and feeds it into the  cclleeaannuupp(8)  daemon.
       Ill-formatted files are deleted without notifying the originator.  This
       program expects to be run from the mmaasstteerr(8) process manager.

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
       None. The ppiicckkuupp(8) daemon does not interact with the outside world.

SSEECCUURRIITTYY
       The  ppiicckkuupp(8)  daemon  is  moderately security sensitive. It runs with
       fixed low privilege and can run in a  chrooted  environment.   However,
       the  program reads files from potentially hostile users.  The ppiicckkuupp(8)
       daemon opens no files for writing, is careful about what files it opens
       for reading, and does not actually touch any data that is sent  to  its
       public service endpoint.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
       Problems and transactions are logged to ssyyssllooggdd(8) or ppoossttllooggdd(8).

BBUUGGSS
       The  ppiicckkuupp(8)  daemon  copies mail from file to the cclleeaannuupp(8) daemon.
       It could avoid message copying overhead by sending  a  file  descriptor
       instead  of  file  data, but then the already complex cclleeaannuupp(8) daemon
       would have to deal with unfiltered user data.

